config DRM_GS_DSIM_CMD
	tristate "Google gs201 DSIM command path for a bootloader display"
	depends on ARCH_EXYNOS || COMPILE_TEST
	depends on OF && DRM
	select DRM_MIPI_DSI
	help
	  Registers a MIPI DSI host on the gs201 (Tensor G2) DSIM so that a
	  panel driver can send DCS commands, for brightness and display
	  on/off, to a panel the bootloader left running. The display
	  pipeline itself stays as the bootloader set it up and is scanned
	  out through simpledrm.

	  This is a bring-up driver until a full DECON/DSIM KMS driver
	  exists. Packets are only sent once the allow_tx module parameter
	  is set.

	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module
	  will be called gs-dsim-cmd.
